// Pull request author: saksham-17
// Change: new rule
// Title: BrokenPipe - Steam LPE SYSTEM Child Outside Install Directory
// Sigma ID: 895d3358-e983-44bf-a69f-0577449c177c
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Saksham Bhattarai
// Date: 2026-10-24 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1068
// Description: Detects steamservice.exe spawning a child process with SYSTEM integrity from an image path
//   outside the standard Steam install directory.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate Steam updates with non-default install paths
//   - Custom Steam library locations outside Program Files
// References:
//   - https://github.com/KillaBoi/BrokenPipe
//   - https://github.com/saksham-17/security-research/blob/d6fcc47335be45804b9183aa2d63640de3b74ba6/BrokenPipe_Technical_Analysis.pdf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/884490cfc07fdc50179717ab172dfa6febfecc80/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_steam_lpe_brokenpipe.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\steamservice.exe" and ProcessIntegrityLevel =~ "System" and (not((FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Steam\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Steam\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\System32\\")))
